{"id": "EUVD-2026-82089", "enisaUuid": "a6193472-8e1c-3438-bb8c-61de1bfced0f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/tegra241-cmdqv: Don't run the error ISR before probe sets up vintfs\n\n__tegra241_cmdqv_probe() requests the error IRQ before it has allocated the\ncmdqv->vintfs array and set cmdqv->num_vintfs. A CMDQV left enabled with a\nlatched error across a kexec fires the IRQ as soon as it is requested, and\ntegra241_cmdqv_isr() then walks the uninitialized cmdqv->vintfs array.\n\nRequest the IRQ only after cmdqv->vintfs is allocated and zeroed, so that\na latched interrupt firing early runs the ISR against a valid array of NULL\nslots that it safely skips.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:03:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1605a56745f22670205f6561df5771bbbb62a99", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f627118b668659c6b195ac48beedb1bf8f53368", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a168254ff8db08f2292be3d8fcbd37d2bb8c3d2d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5acd67ceb38debe2fbf70ea35e2dec9f7ab01bbd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90428", "GHSA-gjw5-xf6c-mcgq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3ab8af61-4cd6-30b2-bd04-24fab14007fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "918eb5c856f6ce4cf93b4b38e4b5e156905c5943 <2f627118b668659c6b195ac48beedb1bf8f53368"}, {"id": "403a78af-38bf-3165-ae9e-698824f5bc4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "55e96bce-756a-3f91-bf79-8c3604795806", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "80439de1-38f1-3823-9815-5427ba3abc71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "839b8959-603b-369b-9674-359003704399", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "918eb5c856f6ce4cf93b4b38e4b5e156905c5943 <5acd67ceb38debe2fbf70ea35e2dec9f7ab01bbd"}, {"id": "b6312e0b-7497-3b8f-a2a1-f2f1a162fc14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "bcc823b5-49d1-302e-8520-1a175ea6301a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "918eb5c856f6ce4cf93b4b38e4b5e156905c5943 <a168254ff8db08f2292be3d8fcbd37d2bb8c3d2d"}, {"id": "c3fc6f9c-3b5c-3a56-be0c-9c72bee5b24b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "f78fd641-22a4-3943-80e1-a8880ad5ae09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "918eb5c856f6ce4cf93b4b38e4b5e156905c5943 <b1605a56745f22670205f6561df5771bbbb62a99"}, {"id": "ff1b739d-3053-3905-9842-be5040789e61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b5fcde78-2a13-3b6d-852b-4e80ebd488f5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}